# Line endings, pinned for the files Linux executes or parses (M8b).
#
# This repository is edited on Windows and deployed to Ubuntu. A shell script checked out
# with CRLF fails on Linux with "bad interpreter: no such file or directory", and a CRLF
# .env gives every variable a trailing carriage return — which would put "\r" on the end
# of a URL or a secret and produce failures that read like anything but a line ending.

* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
env.production.example text eol=lf
